ition  where steppenwolf has mira pinned  against the wall or mira using this  power to suck  blood out of his face yeah the snyder  cut is way bloodier  now i gotta play this for you guys check  out the difference in the two cuts with  the music played when the justice league  arrives to save silas  boring  one left me like a limp noodle and the  other i was like hell yeah baby let's go  there are some other big differences how  this whole rescue operation goes namely  surrounding the flash in the wean  version he has this long speech with  batman about how he's never fought  before so he's relegated to saving the  hostages  this is removed in the snyder cut and he  kind of leads the hostages by themselves  instead of manually picking them up one  by one  plus there's a scene where he saves them  all from flying debris and thank god  they got rid of this totally unnecessary  scene where the flash lands on wonder  woman and it looks like he's humping her  directed by joss whedon the ween cut  also does away with any of the emotion  that comes with cyborg saving his father  whereas in the snyder cut we get  i wasn't sure he'd come you're my father  steppenwolf ends up escaping and  contacting darkseid where he tells him  that earth is where the anti-life  equation is located carved into the very  surface of the world  this equation as he calls it is the  ultimate weapon for controlling all  life throughout the multiverse this is  not in the 2017 version with the justice  league in possession of the third box we  get more backstory on what  exactly it is silas called it a change  machine as it can reinstate particles  they use the analogy of a house burning  down the house doesn't disappear its  particles just turn into something else  like ash and smoke  by this logic the change machine can be  used to bring superman back in the  wheaton cut they're more like hey we can  use this to jumpstart superman and away  they go  minor difference but when the flash  arrives to bruce wayne's bat cave he  flashes around to check it like a giddy  school boy which doesn't happen in the  snyder cut the gravedigging scene here  is  also extended in whedon's cut we never  get to see the interaction between  aquaman and diana here in fact they're  never even shown i found this  interaction between the two  a lot more genuine than the weiner  version where aquaman accidentally sits  on the lasso of truth and professes how  he thinks wonder woman is  cute you're gorgeous the decision to use  the box is questioned in the snyder cut  by alfred who is concerned its power  could have terrible consequences  if you start playing with this little  box of  tricks i mean it could be the end of  everything in the weed cut  this is brought up by diana technology  is like any other power without reason  without heart it destroys us  so the team has to bring superman's  corpse to the kryptonian ship at star  labs in the weed cut they kind of just  walk in there's hardly any security  except for the guy at the front gate and  they go about their business  in the snyder cut it's a whole big deal  they have to create a diversion and get  everyone who's working there out by  creating an alarm we also get a way more  in-depth view of what's in the  kryptonian ship like these different  superman suits and even a dead body  superman's resurrection in snyder's  version is intercut with shots of lois  visiting his memorial for the last time  bringing back that emotional weight to  the scene and setting up how she'll  bring him back to reality the plan to  jumpstart superman is the same in both  versions but just before barry is about  to use his electrical charge  cyborg is bombarded with images of the  future now i won't get into  too much details of what these images  mean but it's clear snyder is setting up  huge things for the dc universe we see  dead diana  dead aquaman who's wearing the king's  crown superman hovering over a dead body  dark side consoling superman and  superman holding batman's cow  it really sets up that superman could  actually be turning evil for good while  the justice league battles superman in  the wean version steppenwolf  comes in and joins the cube and just  takes off as mentioned before this  snyder cut sees him taking it from silas  superman goes off with lois and we get a  more fleshed out version of this reunion  and this magical line  the man's been dead for days one of the  big differences between the two versions  is  knowing superman will come and help the  justice league in the 2017 version it's  a surprise when he arrives to take on  steppenwolf but the snyder cut we know  he's eventually going to come  they wanted me back for a reason  i need to find out why then we get this  great scene where he gets into a new  dark suit as the voices of his real dad  jorel and his adopted dad jonathan kent  give voice over on how he can be a force  for good there's also this scene in the  weeden cut where diana pops a bruised  bruce wayne's shoulder back into place  and we find out it was bruce's idea to  bring in lois to turn  superman not at all what happens in the  snyder cut in deciding what to do next  the snyder cut also took out the scene  where aquaman gets really upset at  cyborg for his malfunction which set off  superman the team sets out with a plan  which is a lot different than whedon's  version here batman will destroy the  dome while the flash creates a band of  energy around the city while cyborg  attempts to desynchronize the cubes  this city itself is also devoid of  citizens while in the weeden cut you'd  get this weird hodgepodge of some shots  having no people at all  while others you'll see them screaming  for their lives the background sky is  totally different too whedon opting to  keep it orangy red while snyder keeps it  night superman even visits alfred in the  snyder cut  likely to find out where the team is  again not in the weeden cut and with  superman's arrival these two versions  differ extremely in the weed cut  superman blows cold air on steppenwolf's  axe and diana breaks it  the cubes are pulled apart and  steppenwolf is defeated there's also  this mini side story where the flash and  superman save the civilians this is all  thrown in the garbage by snyder who  gives us something far more thrilling  while setting up big things for the dcu  the snyder version sees superman beating  the crap out of steppenwolf even ripping  off his horn  but the justice league ultimately fails  and barry who was shot and couldn't pull  off the energy blast has to do something  he's  not supposed to do go faster than the  speed of light and move  back time we see as he moves so fast the  particles start to reform and when he  touches barry  well he's given a weird post-apocalyptic  family welcome  who want him to stay with him forever he  refuses and were transported back a few  moments before the blast that would kill  everyone allowing the entire team to  take a stab at steppenwolf  throwing him back through the portal to  darkseid's homeworld something this  snyder cut made me feel at the end was  that they were finally a team while  simultaneously setting up a conflict for  a sequel darkseid coming to earth to  take the anti-life equation with his  armada snyder's epilogue and post-credit  scenes are more fleshed out as well  in the 2017 version we see how cyborg is  good with his dad now even though little  time was spent on that  aquaman goes back to the water flash  runs around town wonder woman goes back  to stopping criminals and superman  reveals his traditional  colored s the wing cut also has that lex  luthor post credit scene both at the  asylum and  on his yawn the yacht version here  however has lex luthor telling deadshot  to put it plainly  shouldn't we have a league of our own  while in the snyder cut he says this  if you want the batman here is something  that  can help you his name is bruce wayne  this is great for the snyder version  since in that post-apocalyptic scene we  see deadshot has teamed up with batman  the snyder version also does away with  this superman in flash  racing scene in snyder's epilogue we see  cyborg in front of the grave of his  parents  batman catching up with some bad guys a  superman's grey s  and arguably the most talked about  change from the 2017 version  this scene involving batman and the  joker in a post-apocalyptic world i  won't get into too much of analysis of  the scene  that's for a different video but we  learned lots of cool things like how  dark side has taken over  something bad has happened to aquaman  lois and harley quinn are dead  alternate timelines and the arrival of  superman who looks like he wants to kick  the crap out of all of them so those are  some of my  favorite differences between whedon and  snyder's justice leagues what did you  think of the snyder cut and which  differences were your favorite that i  didn't include i want to hear them in  the comments below thanks for watching  everyone make sure to like and subscribe  and for more bad takes you can follow me  on twitter and instagram  think story yt until next time remember  daddy loves you very much


